Theorem RL-24: bidirectional dataflow identifies matching (Inc, Dec) pairs across blocks

  Preconditions:
    - RL-24 governs PRE-style global RC motion pairing per Annex E §AIMS PRE-Style Global RC Motion: "Bidirectional dataflow (bottom-up
      release + top-down retain) SHALL identify matching (Inc, Dec) pairs
      across blocks."
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - RL-24 is a POST-PIPELINE pass over realized IR (PRE = partial-redundancy
      elimination, Clang/LLVM ObjC ARC lineage per Annex E §AIMS
      sec-Advanced-Optimization-Patterns).

  Soundness property:
    Forall RcInc in block B_i and RcDec in block B_d on the same variable v:

      (P1) Matching: RL-24 identifies (B_i, B_d) as a matching pair iff B_d is
           forward-reachable from B_i (the inc's reference reaches the dec)
           AND B_i is backward-reachable from B_d (the dec releases that inc's
           reference). Both directions of the bidirectional dataflow must
           confirm the pairing.

      (P2) Soundness: a pair matched in BOTH directions is a genuine
           inc/release pairing — the inc's created reference is exactly the
           one the dec releases. A pair matched in only one direction is NOT a
           genuine pairing (a forward-only pair has the inc reaching a dec
           that releases a DIFFERENT reference; a backward-only pair has a dec
           whose released reference came from a DIFFERENT inc), so eliminating
           or moving it would unbalance the count.

    RL-24 supplies the matched-pair set that RL-25 then tests for
    eliminability.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the rc_counting engine.

    Part (P1/P2) — bidirectional reachability grid:
      both_directions_matched -> matched (genuine pair)
      forward_only_unmatched -> NOT matched
      backward_only_unmatched -> NOT matched
      neither_unmatched -> NOT matched
      Coverage gate: 4 reachability cases — a pair is matched iff BOTH
      forward and backward reachability hold (the conjunction is the
      bidirectional-dataflow contract).

    Engines dispatched:
      rc_counting (PRIMARY —
        section_08::verify_rl24_bidirectional_pair_matching; bidirectional
        reachability enumeration; emits Fail when a one-directional pair is
        wrongly matched)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      case_analysis (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 rc_counting engine discharges RL-24 via the bidirectional reachability grid (a matched (Inc, Dec) pair requires BOTH forward reachability inc->dec AND backward reachability dec->inc; one-directional pairs are unmatched), the matched-pair set RL-25 consumes for eliminability
